// DF-225b, closed by design 241 unit 1: an UNDEFINED TYPE NAME gets one
// located diagnostic, in every position a type is written.
//
// It used to be one of two silences. Where nothing downstream needed a layout
// the name became an opaque nominal the checker carried, so an annotated `let`,
// a struct FIELD, a `type` alias RHS and a trait REQUIREMENT reported either a
// mismatch against a type that does not exist (``cannot assign `Int` to
// variable of type `Float64` ``, plus a "not `Printable`" cascade) or nothing
// at all. Where a layout WAS needed it reached codegen and died there
// (`internal compiler error: Undefined struct: Float64`) — with no location at
// three of those positions.
//
// `Float64` was the motivating spelling (DF-225c, ruled Aug 20: FLOAT ONLY —
// `Float` is the float type and `Float64` names nothing). Design 240 item 4
// went looking for the `Float64` type-name registration the ruling asked to
// remove and found there is none: `Float64` behaves exactly as any nonsense
// name does, which is the finding. So the compiler half of that ruling is not a
// removal — it is this diagnostic, and this diagnostic is DF-225b's class, not
// one name's.
//
// THE POSITION MATRIX, one row per swept position (design 240 item 4's sweep
// plus DF-225b's original two). The GENERIC BOUND row is the one position that
// already had a clean diagnostic before this brief; it is here so the matrix is
// complete and so a regression in it is caught beside the others.
//
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: undefined type `Float64`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: undefined type `MissingField`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: undefined type `MissingPayload`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: undefined type `MissingSizeof`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: undefined type `MissingParam`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: undefined type `MissingReturn`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: undefined type `MissingAlias`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: undefined type `MissingRequirement`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: unknown trait `MissingBound`
// EXPECT-ERROR-ABSENT: internal compiler error

// alias RHS
type Handle = MissingAlias

// struct field
struct Holder {
    slot: MissingField
}

// enum case payload
enum Reel {
    case Loaded(t: MissingPayload)
    case Empty
}

// trait requirement signature
trait Sink {
    func accept(&self, item: MissingRequirement)
}

// function signature, parameter and return alike
func idn(x: MissingParam) -> MissingReturn { x }

// generic bound
func widest<T: MissingBound>(v: &T) -> Int { 1 }

func main() {
    // let annotation
    let x: Float64 = 1.0
    // sizeof<> type argument
    let n = sizeof<MissingSizeof>()
    print("unreachable {n}")
}
